# The agent-loop-kpi group, lifted VERBATIM out of prometheusrule.yaml (comments stripped — the manifest is its
# one home) — the rules file that agent-loop-kpi.promtool-test loads. Not a manifest and not applied to
# anything: `promtool test rules` needs upstream-format rules (top-level `groups:`), and a
# PrometheusRule keeps them under `.spec`. Named .promtool-rules rather than .yaml on purpose —
# manifest-lint kubeconforms EVERY *.yaml under argocd/resources.
#
# ⚠ Drift-pinned by `devbox run prometheus-rules-lint`'s bidirectional CR↔copy pin — re-copy after
# editing the group:
#
#   yq -o=json '{"groups":[{"name":"agent-loop-kpi","interval":"1h","rules":[.spec.groups[] | select(.name == "agent-loop-kpi") | .rules[]]}]}' argocd/resources/pushgateway/prometheusrule.yaml | yq -P '.'
groups:
  - name: agent-loop-kpi
    interval: 1h
    rules:
      - record: agent_loop:rides_ended:count_7d
        expr: |
          count by (project) (
            count by (project, issue, round) (
              label_replace(label_replace(label_replace(
                max_over_time(kube_pod_status_phase{pod=~"agent-.+-issue-[0-9]+-r[0-9]+",phase=~"Succeeded|Failed"}[7d]) > 0,
                "project", "$1", "namespace", "(.+)"),
                "issue", "$1", "pod", "agent-.+-issue-([0-9]+)-r[0-9]+"),
                "round", "$1", "pod", "agent-.+-issue-[0-9]+-r([0-9]+)")
            )
          )
      - record: agent_loop:rides_unrecorded:count_7d
        expr: |
          count by (project) (
              count by (project, issue, round) (
                label_replace(label_replace(label_replace(
                  max_over_time(kube_pod_status_phase{pod=~"agent-.+-issue-[0-9]+-r[0-9]+",phase=~"Succeeded|Failed"}[7d]) > 0,
                  "project", "$1", "namespace", "(.+)"),
                  "issue", "$1", "pod", "agent-.+-issue-([0-9]+)-r[0-9]+"),
                  "round", "$1", "pod", "agent-.+-issue-[0-9]+-r([0-9]+)")
              )
            unless on (project, issue, round)
              last_over_time(agent_run_total[1h])
          )
          or
          agent_loop:rides_ended:count_7d * 0
      - record: agent_loop:issues_within_two_rounds:ratio_7d
        expr: |
          (
              count by (project) (
                  (count by (project, issue) (count by (project, issue, round) (last_over_time(agent_run_total{role="worker"}[1h]))) <= 2)
                and on (project, issue)
                  (agent_run_total{role="worker"} and on (project, issue, role, round) (time() - push_time_seconds{job="agent_run"}) < 7 * 86400)
              )
            or
              count by (project) (count by (project, issue) (agent_run_total{role="worker"} and on (project, issue, role, round) (time() - push_time_seconds{job="agent_run"}) < 7 * 86400)) * 0
          )
          /
          (count by (project) (count by (project, issue) (agent_run_total{role="worker"} and on (project, issue, role, round) (time() - push_time_seconds{job="agent_run"}) < 7 * 86400)) >= 10)
      - record: agent_loop:queued_within_4h:ratio_7d
        expr: |
          (
              count by (project) (sum by (project, number) (label_replace(count_over_time(github_agent_issue{label="agent/queued"}[7d:5m]), "project", "$1", "repo", "(.+)")) <= 48)
            or
              count by (project) (sum by (project, number) (label_replace(count_over_time(github_agent_issue{label="agent/queued"}[7d:5m]), "project", "$1", "repo", "(.+)"))) * 0
          )
          /
          (count by (project) (sum by (project, number) (label_replace(count_over_time(github_agent_issue{label="agent/queued"}[7d:5m]), "project", "$1", "repo", "(.+)"))) >= 10)
      - alert: AgentRidesUnrecorded
        expr: |
          agent_loop:rides_unrecorded:count_7d > 1
        for: 2h
        labels:
          severity: warning
          triage: dig
        annotations:
          summary: '{{ $value }} worker rides on {{ $labels.project }} ended in the last 7 days without a run record — above the KPI target (at most 1)'
          description: 'agent_loop:rides_unrecorded:count_7d{project="{{ $labels.project }}"} is {{ $value }} (target: at most 1). A ride counts when its pod agent-<project>-issue-<n>-r<round> reached Succeeded or Failed in the 7 d and no agent_run_total series carries the same project, issue and round — the cost boards, the ledger and the retro never saw it. Check: (1) the expression of the record rule without its outer count names each issue and round; (2) the issue''s timeline comment for that round (a strike, a re-dispatch); (3) s3://agent-transcripts/<project>/issue-<n>/ for a worker-r<round>-* prefix — none means the pod died before its finalize step. The KPI and its target are named in docs/agents/observability-and-retro.md §Part D.'
      - alert: AgentLoopRoundsBelowTarget
        expr: |
          agent_loop:issues_within_two_rounds:ratio_7d < 0.6
        for: 6h
        labels:
          severity: warning
          triage: dig
        annotations:
          summary: Less than 60 % of the issues {{ $labels.project }} worked in the last 7 days were done within two worker rounds — below the KPI target
          description: 'agent_loop:issues_within_two_rounds:ratio_7d{project="{{ $labels.project }}"} is {{ $value | humanizePercentage }} (target: at least 60 %; at least 10 issues with a worker run in the 7 d). A round after the first is a PR that came back: changes requested, or a red check. Check: (1) count by (issue) (agent_run_total{project="{{ $labels.project }}",role="worker"}) > 2 names the issues; (2) the reviews on their PRs name what came back; (3) the escape records of the island intake receipts for the same PRs. The KPI and its target are named in docs/agents/observability-and-retro.md §Part D.'
      - alert: AgentLoopQueueWaitBelowTarget
        expr: |
          agent_loop:queued_within_4h:ratio_7d < 0.6
        for: 6h
        labels:
          severity: warning
          triage: dig
        annotations:
          summary: Less than 60 % of the issues queued on {{ $labels.project }} in the last 7 days left the queue within 4 hours — below the KPI target
          description: 'agent_loop:queued_within_4h:ratio_7d{project="{{ $labels.project }}"} is {{ $value | humanizePercentage }} (target: at least 60 %; at least 10 issues carried agent/queued in the 7 d). An issue counts as waiting for every 5 minutes it carries agent/queued, whatever holds it (the WIP cap, a footprint hold, a blockedBy edge). Check: (1) sum by (number) (count_over_time(github_agent_issue{repo="{{ $labels.project }}",label="agent/queued"}[7d:5m])) / 12 > 4 names the issues and their hours; (2) the scan report''s hold line for each; (3) AgentQueueStalled for a wedged dispatcher. The KPI and its target are named in docs/agents/observability-and-retro.md §Part D.'
